# Slice 283 probe: a reached write into an immutable value is the implicit `interpreter`, the handler takes it and the object stays.  Entry 7.
Other:
    int: q 5
end: Other
Holder:
    int: n 1
    Inner:
        int: q 2
    end: Inner
    @: k Other Other
end: Holder
int: Hf 0
fn: write (@: h Holder) int
    ---
        h\k: Other
        return: 11
        catch: interpreter ()
            return: 7
    ---
end: write
fn: m () int
    b: immutable: merge(Holder)
    return: write(b)
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
